From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000: Add UART1

Describe UART1, the Bluetooth UART on A8 handhelds such as the iPod
touch 6 (N102), disabled until a board enables it, with its TX/RX and
RTS/CTS pins (173, 174, 175, 176 in function 1, from the ADT uart1
function-tx and function-rts). Using the apple,t7000-uart compatible
gives it the T8010 oversampling required for high baud rates.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
index 72a2e7d52..9d61c4e8a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000.dtsi
@@ -148,6 +148,18 @@ serial0: serial@20a0c0000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		serial1: serial@20a0c4000 {
+			compatible = "apple,t7000-uart", "apple,t8010-uart", "apple,s5l-uart";
+			reg = <0x2 0x0a0c4000 0x0 0x4000>;
+			reg-io-width = <4>;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 159 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&clkref>, <&clkref>;
+			clock-names = "uart", "clk_uart_baud0";
+			power-domains = <&ps_uart1>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		serial5: serial@20a0d4000 {
 			compatible = "apple,t7000-uart", "apple,t8010-uart", "apple,s5l-uart";
 			reg = <0x2 0x0a0d4000 0x0 0x4000>;
@@ -387,6 +399,13 @@ i2c3_pins: i2c3-pins {
 					 <APPLE_PINMUX(86, 1)>;
 			};
 
+			uart1_pins: uart1-pins {
+				pinmux = <APPLE_PINMUX(173, 1)>,
+					 <APPLE_PINMUX(174, 1)>,
+					 <APPLE_PINMUX(175, 1)>,
+					 <APPLE_PINMUX(176, 1)>;
+			};
+
 			uart5_pins: uart5-pins {
 				pinmux = <APPLE_PINMUX(57, 1)>;
 			};
